system "UN:ukr-Cyrl:Latn:2012" {

metadata {
  authority_id un
  id 2012
  language iso-639-2:ukr
  source_script Cyrl
  destination_script Latn
  name Romanization of Ukrainian (2012)
  url http://www.eki.ee/wgrs/rom1_uk.htm
  creation_date 2010

  notes {
    note "Diffed against the Romanization of Ukrainian for Geographical Names table\n as published in the WGRS Report on the Current Status of UN Romanization Systems\n for Geographical Names, version 4.0 (February 2013) (eki.ee/wgrs/rom1_uk.htm;\n also unstats wgrr4ukranian): all 34 rows verified. The system was approved by\n the UN in 2012 (X/9), based on the national rules adopted 27 January 2010;\n the name previously read 'Belarusian, Russian And Ukrainian Cyrillic (2012)',\n a carry-over from the 1998 map."

    note "Row 4: h, with gh in the romanization of зг (zgh) — encoded by the\n dependency chain's Gh/gh before Зз rules. Rows 8/13/14/31/32: second variant\n (ye/yi/y/yu/ya) word-initially, encoded by the dependency chain's boundary\n rules; the word-initial variants are suppressed after the apostrophe per the\n national rules (not_before boundary + ’). Rows 33/34: ь and ’ are not romanized."
  }
}

